	<p>
		Hello!, I'm Manish, who created RISE out of my fascination with technology, robotics, and the idea of building things that can genuinely help people. What began as a collection of ideas and small experiments gradually turned into something much bigger—a long-term project where I could explore robotics, artificial intelligence, embedded systems, computer vision, and autonomous technology.
	I’m still learning as I build. Many ideas have been tested, broken, redesigned, paused, and started again. Every experiment has taught me something, whether it worked or not.
	RISE is also something I’m developing alongside my academics, so progress isn’t always as fast as I would like. But I see that as part of the journey. I’m learning not only how to build technology, but also how to turn ambitious ideas into systems that can actually work in the real world.
	RISE is still being built. And so am I. 🚀 		
	</p>
	
	<h2>My Journey</h2>
	<p>
		RISE started as an idea that I wanted to turn into something real.
		Over time, that idea grew through experiments with electronics,
		robotics, programming, and AI. Some projects worked, some failed,
		and some had to be put on hold. But every attempt gave me something
		new to learn and pushed me to understand the technology more deeply.
	</p>
	<h2>The Struggles</h2>

	<p>
		Building RISE has not been a straight path. Limited resources,
		difficult technical problems, failed experiments, and the need to
		balance development with academics have all slowed the process.
		Some ideas have had to wait, some prototypes have had to be rebuilt,
		and sometimes the best thing I could do was step back, learn more,
		and try again.
	</p>

